1
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:38,079
Mr. Fang, I'm hungry and sleepy right now.

2
00:01:38,239 --> 00:01:41,480
Do you think it'll eat us?

3
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:44,519
Either it eats us

4
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:47,239
and turns us into poop,

5
00:01:47,719 --> 00:01:49,599
or we eat this poop monster

6
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:51,319
and turn it into poop.

7
00:02:12,319 --> 00:02:13,520
Mom!

8
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:14,879
Come here, come here!

9
00:02:15,719 --> 00:02:17,360
Mr. Fang, I'm done for!

10
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:18,400
Go get another torch!

11
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,639
Bie Fan, go!

12
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:28,680
Mr. Fang! Mom!

13
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:32,319
Go!

14
00:02:33,639 --> 00:02:34,439
Mr. Fang!

15
00:02:36,719 --> 00:02:37,240
Go!

16
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:38,639
Go!

17
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:45,800
Bie Fan, you...

18
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:06,520
Want some grilled snake? Grilled snake.

19
00:03:06,919 --> 00:03:07,960
Mr. Fang.

20
00:03:18,439 --> 00:03:19,319
It's pretty strong!

21
00:03:21,919 --> 00:03:24,000
Mr. Fang, grab its neck!

22
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,039
It's so long, where's its neck?

23
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,360
It's so long! Which part is its neck?

24
00:03:27,919 --> 00:03:29,319
Bie Fan, Bie Fan! Hit its weak spot!

25
00:03:34,719 --> 00:03:36,719
Mr. Fang!

26
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:38,000
Bite it!

27
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,120
Mr. Fang

28
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:25,759
Mr. Fang, why isn't it moving?

29
00:04:27,399 --> 00:04:28,279
You...

30
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:30,720
You wait here.

31
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:31,600
I'll go take a look.

32
00:04:45,759 --> 00:04:46,480
It's dead.

33
00:04:47,759 --> 00:04:48,879
R-Really?

34
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,560
Then h-how did it die?

35
00:04:57,360 --> 00:05:00,199
I... I know. I know now.

36
00:05:00,199 --> 00:05:02,920
Mr. Fang, it died of frustration.

37
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,120
Look inside its mouth,

38
00:05:08,399 --> 00:05:09,720
it's propped open by a stick.

39
00:05:09,959 --> 00:05:11,399
It doesn't have hands,

40
00:05:11,399 --> 00:05:13,680
so it couldn't pull the stick out.

41
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:15,160
So it must've died of frustration.

42
00:05:15,519 --> 00:05:17,959
This snake had a huge temper.

43
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:29,399
You killed a python!

44
00:05:30,839 --> 00:05:33,399
You killed a python!

45
00:05:34,439 --> 00:05:35,439
That's amazing!

46
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,399
You killed a python!

47
00:05:38,639 --> 00:05:39,920
You're amazing!

48
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:41,199
Original! Original! Original!

49
00:05:42,399 --> 00:05:45,000
Then we're both amazing!

50
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,680
We killed a python together!

51
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,279
Mom! Mom!

52
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:01,199
We won't get eaten by it!

53
00:06:01,199 --> 00:06:03,040
We can eat it instead!

54
00:06:12,959 --> 00:06:14,240
That's too fast!

55
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,839
Just spin it faster and you're good.

56
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:30,680
Should I put it all in?

57
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:31,560
Just half is fine.

58
00:06:32,839 --> 00:06:33,879
You're the chef.

59
00:06:34,439 --> 00:06:36,480
Will this even taste good, Mr. Fang?

60
00:06:37,399 --> 00:06:38,519
It's good.

61
00:06:42,639 --> 00:06:44,199
I can't get it out.

62
00:06:44,639 --> 00:06:45,120
Here.

63
00:06:54,639 --> 00:06:55,439
Thanks.

64
00:06:59,639 --> 00:07:00,360
That was delicious.

65
00:07:00,839 --> 00:07:01,560
Maybe this meal

66
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:03,360
is the most delicious meal I've ever had in my life.

67
00:07:03,759 --> 00:07:04,519
What do we call this?

68
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:07,399
This is Rock-Bottom Hotpot.

69
00:07:07,879 --> 00:07:09,040
And we don't even have to wait for a table.

70
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:11,800
It's not bad.

71
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:15,920
I think that hotpot soup base was a bit salty.

72
00:07:16,519 --> 00:07:17,800
When we get out of here,

73
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,079
I'll make some hotpot base for you to try.

74
00:07:22,879 --> 00:07:24,240
You know how to make hotpot base?

75
00:07:24,839 --> 00:07:26,560
I... I'm a chef.

76
00:07:27,399 --> 00:07:30,720
Sichuan cuisine, Cantonese... I can cook anything.

77
00:07:31,399 --> 00:07:32,839
Then what do you think is

78
00:07:32,839 --> 00:07:34,560
the best meal you've ever had in your life?

79
00:07:34,879 --> 00:07:36,040
Mapo Tofu.

80
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:38,519
What's so good about Mapo Tofu?

81
00:07:38,519 --> 00:07:39,319
Let me tell you,

82
00:07:39,519 --> 00:07:40,279
I had the honor

83
00:07:41,279 --> 00:07:42,639
of eating Buddha Jumps Over the Wall once.

84
00:07:44,199 --> 00:07:44,959
It was incredibly delicious.

85
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,920
Mixed with rice, it was absolutely amazing.

86
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:50,160
Mapo Tofu mixed with rice is also delicious.

87
00:07:50,639 --> 00:07:51,680
One is tofu.

88
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:52,879
The other is abalone.

89
00:07:52,959 --> 00:07:54,000
One is home-style.

90
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:54,839
The other is a famous delicacy.

91
00:07:54,839 --> 00:07:56,680
In terms of their level and price,

92
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,360
they're completely different.

93
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:58,439
How can you even compare them?

94
00:07:58,439 --> 00:08:00,000
Mapo Tofu tastes better!

95
00:08:01,399 --> 00:08:02,360
Buddha Jumps Over the Wall tastes better!

96
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:03,680
Mapo Tofu tastes better!

97
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:04,639
Buddha Jumps Over the Wall tastes better!

98
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:05,639
Mapo Tofu tastes better!

99
00:08:05,639 --> 00:08:06,600
Why are you so stubborn?

100
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,560
Why are you so stubborn? I...

101
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,360
All the energy I got from that snake went into arguing with you!

102
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,399
Why are you so stubborn?

103
00:08:11,519 --> 00:08:13,360
Tell me, what makes Mapo Tofu so good?

104
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:15,079
Come on, let's hear it.

105
00:08:18,639 --> 00:08:19,959
Mapo Tofu.

106
00:08:20,279 --> 00:08:23,240
First, add a decent amount of oil to the wok.

107
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:24,959
Peanut oil is the best.

108
00:08:25,319 --> 00:08:27,160
Peanut oil is fragrant.

109
00:08:27,879 --> 00:08:30,519
Once the oil is hot, add the minced meat.

110
00:08:31,079 --> 00:08:33,159
Once the minced meat changes color,

111
00:08:33,279 --> 00:08:35,639
add a spoonful of cooking wine to remove the raw smell.

112
00:08:35,799 --> 00:08:38,120
When the minced meat is fried golden brown,

113
00:08:38,519 --> 00:08:40,759
then add two spoonfuls of broad bean paste.

114
00:08:41,279 --> 00:08:42,840
Remember, Bie Fan,

115
00:08:42,919 --> 00:08:44,159
it's two spoonfuls.

116
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:46,480
Too much, and it'll be too salty.

117
00:08:46,799 --> 00:08:50,120
After frying the bean paste until the red oil comes out,

118
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:53,080
add the chilies and minced garlic.

119
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:55,200
Then add some water,

120
00:08:55,519 --> 00:08:58,600
light soy sauce, dark soy sauce, and the tofu.

121
00:08:58,919 --> 00:09:00,440
Add a bit more water.

122
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:04,399
After simmering on low heat for five minutes,

123
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:07,039
we add it in two batches...

124
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:07,879
Two batches.

125
00:09:08,519 --> 00:09:11,399
Cornstarch slurry. One spoonful.

126
00:09:13,799 --> 00:09:15,399
Two spoonfuls. Good.

127
00:09:18,159 --> 00:09:19,440
Right before taking it out of the wok,

128
00:09:19,679 --> 00:09:22,879
add a little chili powder.

129
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:25,200
And a bit of chopped green onion.

130
00:09:26,279 --> 00:09:27,960
See? Did you get all that?

131
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:31,600
The Mapo Tofu my mom makes

132
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,000
is the best in the world.

133
00:09:41,279 --> 00:09:42,360
I think you're right.

134
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:44,399
This Mapo Tofu

135
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:47,120
must taste better than Buddha Jumps Over the Wall.

136
00:09:50,279 --> 00:09:50,919
Yeah.

137
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:57,279
Bie Fan, what's your lifelong wish?

138
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:59,399
I want to take a shower.

139
00:09:59,399 --> 00:10:00,759
I haven't showered for days.

140
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,159
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

141
00:10:02,159 --> 00:10:02,960
I want to take a shower too.

142
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,120
We stink. This smell.

143
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:06,120
I mean, do you have any bigger wishes?

144
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:08,840
I want to take a bath.

145
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:10,519
Does it have to be about personal hygiene?

146
00:10:11,879 --> 00:10:13,559
I... I mean, like...

147
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:15,200
just...

148
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,120
like, in your whole life,

149
00:10:18,799 --> 00:10:19,799
the thing you want to do most.

150
00:10:24,639 --> 00:10:26,440
Watch the flag-raising ceremony at Tiananmen.

151
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,399
That's a good wish.

152
00:10:29,639 --> 00:10:30,559
Just watch the flag-raising?

153
00:10:31,519 --> 00:10:33,399
I haven't thought about anything else yet.

154
00:10:34,039 --> 00:10:35,000
Mr. Fang,

155
00:10:35,279 --> 00:10:37,279
in your life so far,

156
00:10:37,279 --> 00:10:39,399
is there something you've always wanted to do?

157
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:40,960
Me?

158
00:10:42,759 --> 00:10:44,639
Have everyone read my poetry collection.

159
00:10:46,279 --> 00:10:47,039
And then?

160
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:53,039
Then the collection becomes a bestseller.

161
00:10:53,919 --> 00:10:54,679
Selling 100 million copies.

162
00:10:55,519 --> 00:10:56,720
And then what?

163
00:10:57,919 --> 00:10:58,840
There's an "and then"?

164
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:02,759
This conversation is getting fun.

165
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:04,840
The book has already sold 100 million copies.

166
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,120
Shouldn't we have some ambition?

167
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,000
Then,

168
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:10,000
my poetry collection

169
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:11,799
gets rated on the platforms,

170
00:11:11,799 --> 00:11:13,120
and it has to be over a 9.

171
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:14,039
But not a perfect 10.

172
00:11:14,039 --> 00:11:16,200
A perfect 10 means no room to grow,

173
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:17,200
no room to progress either.

174
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:19,240
Then everyone's comments below would be,

175
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:21,279
"This Fang Haowen is so talented.

176
00:11:21,279 --> 00:11:22,679
We totally misjudged him before.

177
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:24,399
A masterpiece!"

178
00:11:25,919 --> 00:11:26,919
And then what?

179
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,080
And then...

180
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:31,039
And then, I'd have to...

181
00:11:31,039 --> 00:11:33,440
win the Nobel Prize in Literature, of course!

182
00:11:34,159 --> 00:11:35,679
But this Nobel Prize in Literature,

183
00:11:35,679 --> 00:11:36,759
shouldn't be too easy to win.

184
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:38,159
It has to carry weight.

185
00:11:38,399 --> 00:11:39,600
For example, the people competing with me

186
00:11:40,159 --> 00:11:41,360
must all be big shots.

187
00:11:41,759 --> 00:11:42,679
Like, for instance,

188
00:11:42,679 --> 00:11:43,519
you know, what's his name...

189
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:44,639
Mo Yan,

190
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:46,440
Haruki Murakami,

191
00:11:46,519 --> 00:11:47,200
Yu Hua.

192
00:11:47,679 --> 00:11:48,440
When the time comes,

193
00:11:48,879 --> 00:11:50,200
we'll all be at the award ceremony.

194
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:51,200
We'll all be sitting in the audience,

195
00:11:51,639 --> 00:11:52,200
sitting in a row,

196
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:53,039
in suits and ties,

197
00:11:53,039 --> 00:11:53,879
looking totally sharp.

198
00:11:54,639 --> 00:11:55,360
And then,

199
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:57,480
feeling extremely nervous,

200
00:11:58,039 --> 00:11:59,960
not knowing who will finally win.

201
00:12:00,879 --> 00:12:02,240
Suddenly, my name is announced.

202
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,159
My expression then: shocked!

203
00:12:05,519 --> 00:12:06,879
Then confident.

204
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,159
Winning is a sure thing.

205
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,240
And after winning the prize?

206
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:15,600
After winning?

207
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,519
After winning...

208
00:12:20,519 --> 00:12:22,200
I'll walk right up to Jin Furong.

209
00:12:22,679 --> 00:12:25,039
I'll walk up to the people who insulted me.

210
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:27,840
I'll walk up to the people who sold me out.

211
00:12:28,039 --> 00:12:30,600
I'll walk up to the people who exploited me.

212
00:12:30,919 --> 00:12:32,320
Then I'll hold up my trophy,

213
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:33,320
and I'll ask them...

214
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:34,440
I'll say, "Am I

215
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:37,039
truly talented or not?"

216
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:42,159
And they'll say yes.

217
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,200
And then?

218
00:12:48,639 --> 00:12:49,360
And then...

219
00:12:58,720 --> 00:12:59,679
I'll just forgive them.

220
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:03,200
Then you'll be happy.

221
00:13:14,879 --> 00:13:16,279
Can I get a refill?

222
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:17,039
Sure.

223
00:13:17,879 --> 00:13:18,679
Thanks.

224
00:13:20,759 --> 00:13:21,759
Once we get out of here,

225
00:13:23,279 --> 00:13:24,480
make me some Mapo Tofu.

226
00:13:27,159 --> 00:13:28,200
I'll take you to watch the flag raising.

227
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:31,600
Here.

228
00:13:32,799 --> 00:13:34,039
Thanks.

229
00:13:36,919 --> 00:13:39,879
So when are we getting out?

230
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:43,120
That massive chunk of old snake meat

231
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:44,240
is enough to feed us for months.

232
00:13:45,639 --> 00:13:46,720
Maybe we'll get out tomorrow.

233
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:50,600
It's been two months.

234
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:52,320
In a huge forest full of wild beasts,

235
00:13:52,559 --> 00:13:54,919
the chances of survival are really slim.

236
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,480
It's only been two months.

237
00:13:57,039 --> 00:13:58,360
Just two months, that's all.

238
00:13:58,519 --> 00:13:59,559
We confirmed it last time,

239
00:13:59,559 --> 00:14:00,919
they're somewhere in this forest.

240
00:14:01,159 --> 00:14:02,399
We just need to keep looking!

241
00:14:02,919 --> 00:14:04,320
We have to find them, dead or alive.

242
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:05,039
Let's go look for them again!

243
00:14:05,039 --> 00:14:05,720
Mr. Rong,

244
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:06,600
over the past few months,

245
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:07,679
the police have invested

246
00:14:07,679 --> 00:14:08,960
a massive amount of resources

247
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:11,200
into searching for Fang Haowen and Bie Fan.

248
00:14:11,559 --> 00:14:13,360
Right now, there really are no useful leads.

249
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:14,360
The investigation has hit a dead end.

250
00:14:14,519 --> 00:14:16,480
Based on standard procedures and overall schedules,

251
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:17,600
our search operations

252
00:14:17,759 --> 00:14:18,759
will have to be suspended for now.

253
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,879
If there are any new developments,

254
00:14:20,879 --> 00:14:21,879
we will notify you immediately.

255
00:14:22,519 --> 00:14:23,360
We ask for your understanding.

256
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:31,440
Bie Fan!

257
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,360
Bie Fan

258
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,399
The sun is out.

259
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:49,679
Time to get some sun.

260
00:14:49,679 --> 00:14:50,399
Coming.

261
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:02,759
Mr. Fang.

262
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:05,559
We only have so much time each day.

263
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:07,600
Where was I? Right.

264
00:15:09,799 --> 00:15:11,639
Chapter 53.

265
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:14,679
It says Tang Sanzang and his three disciples

266
00:15:15,279 --> 00:15:18,639
arrived at Xiliang Women's Kingdom.

267
00:15:19,039 --> 00:15:22,360
Tang Sanzang and Zhu Bajie were thirsty,

268
00:15:22,679 --> 00:15:23,720
and wanted some water.

269
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:28,919
So they drank from the Pregnancy River.

270
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:30,759
Guess what happened?

271
00:15:31,679 --> 00:15:34,799
Their stomachs started hurting.

272
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:37,159
You might think,

273
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:38,519
they needed to poop.

274
00:15:38,679 --> 00:15:39,639
Nope.

275
00:15:40,200 --> 00:15:44,720
Drinking from the Pregnancy River makes you pregnant.

276
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:49,080
You have to give birth.

277
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:55,840
Drink the water and you get pregnant?

278
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:58,000
And have to give birth?

279
00:16:00,759 --> 00:16:02,240
Bie Fan, have you never dated anyone?

280
00:16:07,279 --> 00:16:08,519
I'm still young.

281
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:11,200
I haven't thought about that yet.

282
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:13,840
We never talked about this before.

283
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:14,919
